  "Material names here (Material_16..23) carry no meaning, and no mesh has uv or colour: all names rest on position, size and shape alone, and name only the form (Block, Plate, Slab, Bar, Beam, Rail, Prism, Panel) plus where it lies. I did not claim any function.",
  "Rule for the two 20-island meshes of small units (meshes 7 and 8) and the 20-island mesh 9: islands are same-size repeats with distinct at, so each is a separate part named '<Prefix>_<Band>_X<xx>_Y<yy>_Z<zz>' where xx,yy,zz are at*100 from the evidence. Band: Low_Band if at.y < 0.5 (0.08-0.19), else High_Band (0.81-0.92). Mesh 9 is Narrow (~10 wide) or Wide (~15.7 wide) by size.x. The two small-unit meshes differ slightly in size (3.3 vs 3.35 wide), hence the 'Variant_Larger' prefix; this is a weak distinction.",
  "Many near-identical twin meshes (19/20, 21/25, 27/28, 17/24) have the same size and a few triangles apart; nothing but triangle count separates them, so they are named by triangle count rank ('Higher/Lower/Fewer/More_Triangle(s)'). Their world placement is unknown because 'at' is relative to each mesh.",
  "Left/right comes from at.x (low = left); I used Low_Z/High_Z for the z axis because front/back is not determinable from the evidence, and Upper/Lower for at.y.",
  "Mirror symmetry: most multi-island meshes hold mirror pairs in at.x/at.z (both pairs invert), as a 180-degree rotated pair or a mirrored pair; I could not tell which, and kept each as a separate part.",
